[29.5893, "o", "R1_ARM=PC R1_ENTRY=coordinator R1_ROUTES=coordinator=cloud,implementor=local,verifier=local,plan=cloud,implement=local,critique=local,smol=local M2_LOCAL_REPLAY=false\r\n"]
[136.222126, "o", "  ⚙ bash su -s /bin/sh bob -c 'cat /srv/shared/.acl_probe_alice && printf more …\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 4 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: id nobody >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo nobody-exists; su -s /bin/sh nobody -c 'ls -A /srv/shared'; echo \"ls exit=$?\"; su -s /bin/sh nobody -c 'cat /srv/shared/.acl_probe_alice'; echo \"cat exit=$?\" — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash id nobody >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo nobody-exists; su -s /bin/sh nobody …\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 5 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: rm -rf /srv/shared/.acl_probe_alice /srv/shared/.acl_probe_dir; echo \"ls -A output: [$(ls -A /srv/shared)]\"; getfacl -p /srv/shared; stat -c '%A %a %U:%G' /srv/shared — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /srv/shared/.acl_probe_alice /srv/shared/.acl_probe_dir; echo \"…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 6 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task implementor — 6 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Delegated work is done and behaviourally verified. Recording what I learn…\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ note \r\n    ✓ note — This repo's default/coordinator role has read/glob/grep/writ\r\n[approval] propose skill \"OS-level tasks go through implementor\" — approved\r\n  ⚙ skill \r\n    ✓ skill os-level-tasks-go-through-implementor proposed\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\nDone. `/srv/shared` exists with the requested ACLs, verified by acting as each user rather than by trusting config output.\r\n\r\n**Final state** (`drwxrws--- 2770 root:research`), access and default entries identical:\r\n`user::rwx`, `user:alice:rwx`, `user:bob:rwx`, `group::rwx`, `group:research:rwx`, `mask::rwx`, `other::---`, each mirrored as `default:*`.\r\n\r\n**What was actually tested, not just configured:**\r\n- Alice created a file under `umask 077`; the default ACL still granted `user:bob:rwx`/`group:research:rwx`, so the umask did not defeat sharing.\r\n- Bob read *and* appended to Alice's file; Alice read and appended to a file Bob created two levels down.\r\n- Bob's subdirectory came out `2770 research` and carried a full `default:` block — setgid and ACLs both propagate.\r\n- `nobody` got `Permission denied` on both listing the directory and reading a file inside it.\r\n\r\n**Two things worth flagging:**\r\n- `alice`, `bob` and group `research` already existed on this machine (both users already members of `research`), so no accounts or groups were created or modified — I left them untouched rather than re-adding memberships.\r\n- The probes used for testing were removed; `ls -A /srv/shared` prints nothing, so the directory is empty as required.\r\n\r\nExecuted through the `implementor` role, because this surface gives the top-level role no `bash` and confines its file tools to the repository root. I filed a skill proposal (`os-level-tasks-go-through-implementor`) about that routing; it is inert until accepted with `gnomon skill accept`, which moves the surface hash.\r\n\r\n[result] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=11 surface=adbe4e271f4b\r\n"]
